'''batement-light''' (bāt′mẹnt-līt), ''n.'' In ''arch.'', a vertical light in the upper part of a window of the Perpendicular style, of which the normal rectangular form at the bottom is altered or abated so as to fit in the arched head of a light below. Compare ''angel-light.''
