'''batestone''' (bāt′stōn), ''n.'' [< ''bate''<sup>5</sup> + ''stone.''] A curved scouring-stone used in bating hides.
{{smaller block|When the hides have been properly worked with the ''batestone'', they are placed in a wash-wheel and worked for about twenty minutes.
{{right|''C. T. Davis'', Leather, p. 586.}}}}

